==English==

===Etymology===
{{uder|en|la|absistere}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|absistō||desist}}; from {{m|la|ab||from, away from}} + {{m|la|sistō||stand}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/əbˈsɪst/|/æbˈsɪst/}}
* {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-absist.wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪst|s=2}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|obsolete}} To stand apart from; to leave off; to [[desist]].
#* '''1603-16''', {{w|Walter Raleigh}}, ''The History of the World''.
#*: They promise to '''absist''' from their purpose of making a war.

